\newlabel{def:c23-access}{{25.2.2}{1531}{The access operation}{tcb@cnt@definition.25.2.2}{}}
\newlabel{lst:c23-lct-core}{{25.2.1}{1531}{The LCT core: is-root test, push-up, rotate, splay, access, findroot. Aux children are ls/rs; fa doubles as path-parent for an aux root. NO makeroot/reverse tag in this rooted section. ASCII only}{lstlisting.25.2.1}{}}
\@writefile{lol}{\contentsline {lstlisting}{\numberline {25.2.1}{\ignorespaces The LCT core: is-root test, push-up, rotate, splay, access, findroot. Aux children are ls/rs; fa doubles as path-parent for an aux root. NO makeroot/reverse tag in this rooted section. ASCII only}}{1531}{lstlisting.25.2.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {25.2.1}{\ignorespaces The running forest \(R\) of \(Figure~\ref {fig:c23-tree}\) after \texttt  {access(7)}. The solid orange preferred path \(1\!-\!2\!-\!5\!-\!7\) is a single auxiliary splay (aux nodes in orange, ordered by depth). The three off-path subtrees \(\{3,8\}\), \(\{4\}\), \(\{6\}\) are their own preferred paths; each path's top node keeps a dashed \emph  {path-parent} pointer into the spine (\(3\!\to \!1\), \(4\!\to \!2\), \(6\!\to \!5\)). These dashed pointers are \(\mathit  {fa}\) links that are \emph  {not} aux children -- that is exactly what \texttt  {is\_root} tests.}}{1531}{figure.caption.267}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:c23-aux}{{25.2.1}{1531}{The running forest \(R\) of \(\figref {c23-tree}\) after \code {access(7)}. The solid orange preferred path \(1\!-\!2\!-\!5\!-\!7\) is a single auxiliary splay (aux nodes in orange, ordered by depth). The three off-path subtrees \(\{3,8\}\), \(\{4\}\), \(\{6\}\) are their own preferred paths; each path's top node keeps a dashed \emph {path-parent} pointer into the spine (\(3\!\to \!1\), \(4\!\to \!2\), \(6\!\to \!5\)). These dashed pointers are \(\mathit {fa}\) links that are \emph {not} aux children -- that is exactly what \code {is\_root} tests}{figure.caption.267}{}}
